      "message": "Dear Maintainers,\nI recently encountered a kernel panic issue and would like to discuss it with you in depth.\nI used the simpleperf tool on an Android device to record CPU performance data for an application over a specified period of time. However, this operation has a probability of triggering a kernel panic. The panic information is as follows. I also tested the same operation on devices with kernel versions 5.10.209 and 5.15.178, and the results were consistent: In both kernel versions, the operation would trigger a kernel panic.\n\n\nCommand:\nam start com.smile.gifmaker; simpleperf record --app com.smile.gifmaker -e cpu-cycles --duration 2 -f 1000 --call-graph dwarf -o /data/local/tmp/perf.data \u0026\n\n\nPanic information:\n[  650.825586][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 000000000000008c\n[  650.832920][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]Mem abort info:\n[  650.836527][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  ESR \u003d 0x96000046\n[  650.842953][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  EC \u003d 0x25: DABT (current EL), IL \u003d 32 bits\n[  650.848593][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  SET \u003d 0, FnV \u003d 0\n[  650.848596][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  EA \u003d 0, S1PTW \u003d 0\n[  650.848598][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]Data abort info:\n[  650.848600][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  ISV \u003d 0, ISS \u003d 0x00000046\n[  650.848602][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]  CM \u003d 0, WnR \u003d 1\n[  650.848605][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026]user pgtable: 4k pages, 39-bit VAs, pgdp\u003d00000001af845000\n[  650.848608][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:fault\u0026][000000000000008c] pgd\u003d00000001af844003, p4d\u003d00000001af844003, pud\u003d00000001af844003, pmd\u003d0000000000000000\n[  650.848620][T125385] FrescoIoBoundEx: [name:traps\u0026]Internal