      "message": "\nWe just need to pay attention to the following two lines of log information:\nUnable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 000000000000008c\npc : [0xffffffe8bb24bdbc] inherit_task_group+0x13c/0x264\n\n\nUsing crash-tool to analyze this panic, the process is as follows:\ncrash_arm64\u003e struct -ox perf_event.group_generation\nstruct perf_event {\n   [0x8c] unsigned int group_generation;\n}\ncrash_arm64\u003e p 0x13c\n$3 \u003d 316\ncrash_arm64\u003e disassemble /s inherit_task_group\n...\n12817   in /work/hupu/code/kernel-5.10/kernel/events/core.c\n12818   in /work/hupu/code/kernel-5.10/kernel/events/core.c\n12819   in /work/hupu/code/kernel-5.10/kernel/events/core.c\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdb8 \u003c+312\u003e:   ldr     w8, [x21, #140]\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdbc \u003c+316\u003e:   str     w8, [x23, #140]\t\t\t//A panic occurred during the execution of a write operation.\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdc0 \u003c+320\u003e:   mov     w23, wzr\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdc4 \u003c+324\u003e:   b       0xffffffe8bb24be28 \u003cinherit_task_group+424\u003e\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdc8 \u003c+328\u003e:   mov     x24, x21\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdcc \u003c+332\u003e:   ldr     x25, [x24, #16]!\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdd0 \u003c+336\u003e:   b       0xffffffe8bb24bdd8 \u003cinherit_task_group+344\u003e\n   0xffffffe8bb24bdd4 \u003c+340\u003e:   ldr     x25, [x25]\n\nIn kernel version 5.10.209, the source code for inherit_group is as follows:\n12790static int inherit_group(struct perf_event *parent_event,\n12791\t      struct task_struct *parent,\n12792\t      struct perf_event_context *parent_ctx,\n12793\t      struct task_struct *child,\n12794\t      struct perf_event_context *child_ctx)\n12795{\n12796\tstruct perf_event *leader;\n12797\tstruct perf_event *sub;\n12798\tstruct perf_event *child_ctr;\n12799\n12800\tleader \u003d inherit_event(parent_event, parent, parent_ctx,\n12801\t\t\t\t child, NULL, child_ctx);\n12802\tif (IS_ERR(leader))\n12803\t\treturn PTR_ERR(leader);\n12804\t/*\n12805\t * @leader can be NULL here because of is_orphaned_event(). In this\n12806\t * case inherit_event() will create individual events, similar to what\n12807\t * perf_group_detach() would do anyway.\n12808\t */\n12809\tfor_each_sibling_event(sub, parent_event) {\n12810\t\tchild_ctr \u003d inherit_event(sub, parent, parent_ctx,\n12811\t\t\t\t\t    child, leader, child_ctx);\n12812\t\tif (IS_ERR(child_ctr))\n12813\t\t\treturn PTR_ERR(child_ctr);\n12814\n12815\t\tif (sub-\u003eaux_event \u003d\u003d parent_event \u0026\u0026 child_ctr \u0026\u0026\n12816\t\t    !perf_get_aux_event(child_ctr, leader))\n12817\t\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n12818\t}\n12819\tleader-\u003egroup_generation \u003d parent_event-\u003egroup_generation;\n12820\treturn 0;\n12821}\n\nTherefore, it can be determined that the panic was triggered during the execution of the following operation, at which point the X23 register contains the value of the leader variable, and the leader is currently NULL.\n12819\tleader-\u003egroup_generation \u003d parent_event-\u003egroup_generation;\n\n\nAlthough the validity of the leader has been judged by IS_ERR at line 12802, it seems that this panic issue indicates that this is not enough. In addition to checking IS_ERR, it is also necessary to check whether the leader is NULL. \ndiff --git a/kernel/events/core.c b/kernel/events/core.c\nindex 3fdecb5e9969..25c2a0bb3116 100644\n--- a/kernel/events/core.c\n+++ b/kernel/events/core.c\n@@ -12816,7 +12816,10 @@ static int inherit_group(struct perf_event *parent_event,\n                    !perf_get_aux_event(child_ctr, leader))\n                        return -EINVAL;\n        }\n-       leader-\u003egroup_generation \u003d parent_event-\u003egroup_generation;\n+\n+       if (leader)\n+               leader-\u003egroup_generation \u003d parent_event-\u003egroup_generation;\n+\n        return 0;\n }\n\n\nI have also made the same changes on devices for kernel-5.10.209 and kernel-5.15.178, and it has proven effective.",
